            "summary": "Six months after Trump warned states off AI regulation, more states than ever are passing their own laws: Connecticut enacted a sweeping AI framework covering companion chatbots and employment decisions, Louisiana became the 22nd state with a consumer data privacy law, and Colorado revised its landmark AI act to take effect January 2027. A discussion draft of the 'Great American AI Act' aims to preempt state rules for three years but has yet to advance. The FTC, meanwhile, has already settled with three marketing firms over deceptive AI capability claims, proving enforcement is moving with or without new federal legislation.",
