            "summary": "The European Commission published a new Code of Practice today requiring consumer-facing AI content to be clearly marked and labelled, extending EU AI governance well beyond the AI Act's original scope. The move closes a gap that allowed companies to defer content-transparency obligations, and signals that the Commission intends to enforce disclosure norms through multiple overlapping instruments. Organizations that have been waiting on AI Act timelines now face a new, parallel compliance track.",
