            "title": "AI prompts are now fair game in court discovery",
            "summary": "A federal magistrate judge in Conservation Law Foundation v. Shell Oil ruled that the AI prompts an expert used to prepare her report must be produced in discovery, treating them as part of the expert's methodology rather than protected drafting material. The decision is one of the clearest signals yet that courts view AI-assisted expert work as fully subject to adversarial scrutiny. Litigators relying on AI tools for expert analysis should assume their prompt histories are discoverable.",
