            "title": "Colorado's AI Act deadline is three weeks away \u2014 and nobody agrees",
            "summary": "Colorado's AI Act enforcement is set for June 30, 2026, but the state legislature is simultaneously weighing a full repeal and a reset to January 2027 under a revised framework. The tension mirrors a national standoff: the Trump administration wants to preempt state AI laws it considers innovation-limiting, while California, Texas, and Connecticut have already enacted their own frameworks. Engineering and legal teams have no clear answer on which rules will actually apply.",
