            "summary": "House members released a discussion draft of the Great American AI Act, a bipartisan bill that would create an AI Standards and Innovation Center inside the Department of Commerce and require frontier AI developers to publish safety frameworks, report incidents, and accept independent audits. Crucially, it would preempt state AI model regulations for three years after enactment, setting up a direct clash with state-level efforts. The bill reflects Congress's growing appetite to establish federal guardrails before the 2027 session.",
