            "summary": "Reps. Jay Obernolte and Lori Trahan dropped a 269-page bipartisan discussion draft of the Great American AI Act, the most sweeping federal AI governance proposal to date. Its headline provision would preempt all state AI development regulations \u2014 including California's suite of bills and Colorado's Act scheduled to take effect June 30 \u2014 for three years. Companies with over $500 million in revenue would have to publish Frontier AI Frameworks, report safety incidents, submit to audits, and fund a $100 million federal AI standards center.",
