            "title": "Connecticut's sweeping AI law is the new state benchmark",
            "summary": "Connecticut enacted SB 5 on May 27, 2026, covering automated employment decisions, AI companion chatbots, synthetic media, and frontier AI whistleblower protections \u2014 analysts called it the most extensive state AI law enacted to date. The law adds to a growing patchwork that now includes new Illinois employment AI rules, Louisiana's comprehensive consumer privacy law (the 22nd US state to pass one), and Colorado's revised AI Act replacing its original landmark legislation. Multi-state companies now face genuinely incompatible obligations with no federal floor in sight.",
