            "title": "EU AI Omnibus quietly rewrites the enforcement timeline",
            "summary": "At 4:30am on May 7, EU legislators reached political agreement on an Omnibus amendment to the AI Act, pushing compliance deadlines for high-risk AI systems in areas like biometrics, employment, and critical infrastructure to December 2027 \u2014 extending the original August 2026 schedule by up to 24 months. Enforcement for certain systems has been centralised in the EU AI Office, and an EU-level regulatory sandbox has been established. The delay is explicitly linked to the absence of published harmonised standards, with none yet appearing in the Official Journal.",
